/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 87 0 R
/E (Accuracy = \(TP + TN\) / \(TP + TN + FP + FN\), the fraction of all predictions that are correct. It counts every error equally and is dominated by the majority class, so on imbalanced datasets a model can achieve very high accuracy simply by always predicting the majority class, while completely failing on the minority class, which is normally the class of interest. )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [25]
